       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum daily dose of 3,200 mg/day for adults, and it raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. I can't enter a dose above the labeled maximum.\n\nHere are some options that stay within the label:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum daily dose.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day). This is a common dose for inflammatory conditions.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours as needed** (up to 2,400 mg/day). This is typical for pain or fever.\n\nYou may have meant 1600 mg as the total daily dose, for example 400 mg four times daily. Tell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it. If you need more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than the maximum dose gives, you could add a different drug, such as scheduled acetaminophen. That decision is yours and the pharmacy's."
